The current composition presents a significant challenge for the [[Ikazaki Cabinet]]. While the SCP-OSP-SDP coalition holds a 13-seat supermajority in the House of Commoners (251 of 475), it controls only 53 of 251 seats in the House of Officers—a substantial minority. The PPO, despite its collapse in the lower house, remains the largest party in the upper house with 100 seats, followed by the LDP with 68. This means the governing coalition will need to negotiate with opposition parties to pass legislation through the upper house, or rely on the two-thirds override in the lower house for bills that the upper house rejects.

The PPO's continued dominance in the upper house reflects the fact that the July 2025 half-election occurred before both the "March Maelstrom" and the [[Satori AI Blackout Crisis]]—the two events that destroyed the PPO's lower house position. The next half-election in July 2028 will be the first opportunity for the upper house's composition to reflect the post-2026 political realignment.

